; Water reflection: first 16 of the 32 LDIs that copy one pixel line
;
; The chain of #R$ADA1-#R$ADE0 copies up to 32 bytes from (HL) to (DE) and counts BC down. The JR at #R$AD9F of
; #R$AD88 enters it 2 x (32 - width) bytes after its start so that exactly `width` (at most 32, LDI_CHAIN_LEN) bytes
; are copied, then execution runs on into #R$ADC1, which ends with the second half of the chain. Falls through to
; #R$ADC1 after the 16th LDI.
@label=WaterCopyChain
c$ADA1 LDI           ; the chain: 32 LDIs from here to #R$ADE0
 $ADA3 LDI           ;
 $ADA5 LDI           ;
 $ADA7 LDI           ;
 $ADA9 LDI           ;
 $ADAB LDI           ;
 $ADAD LDI           ;
 $ADAF LDI           ;
 $ADB1 LDI           ;
 $ADB3 LDI           ;
 $ADB5 LDI           ;
 $ADB7 LDI           ;
 $ADB9 LDI           ;
 $ADBB LDI           ;
 $ADBD LDI           ;
 $ADBF LDI           ;
